From: Research Team <research@example.local>
Date: Sun, 3 May 2026 14:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 0001/0003] RFC: mm: add semantic reclaim helper

// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
/* RFC ONLY – NOT FOR SUBMISSION */

This patch introduces a helper function 'vma_semantic_hint(vma)' to safely
retrieve the recorded semantic intent for a given VMA.

This provides the foundation for the reclaim path to query the
intended memory behavior (streaming, reuse, ephemeral) before
making aging or eviction decisions.

Signed-off-by: Research Team <research@example.local>
---
 include/linux/mm.h | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/linux/mm.h b/include/linux/mm.h
index 8d28f802e2c1..9d28f802e2c1 100644
--- a/include/linux/mm.h
+++ b/include/linux/mm.h
@@ -272,6 +272,12 @@ extern unsigned int kobj_max_free_obj(struct kobject *kobj);
 #define VM_SEMANTIC_EPHEMERAL	3
 /* End RFC */
 
+/* RFC: Helper to get semantic hint from VMA */
+static inline u8 vma_semantic_hint(struct vm_area_struct *vma)
+{
+	return vma->vm_semantic_hint;
+}
+
 #ifndef VM_GROWSUP
 #define VM_GROWSUP	VM_NONE
 #endif
